    raw_easy = [('Under the PM-KISAN scheme, what total annual income support is provided to eligible farmer families?', 'Rs 6,000 per year in three equal installments of Rs 2,000', ['Rs 12,000 per year in monthly installments', 'Rs 5,000 per year in single payment', 'Rs 10,000 per year in two installments'], 'PM-KISAN transfers Rs 6,000 annually directly into bank accounts in three four-monthly tranches of Rs 2,000.'), ('What is the primary objective of the Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (Ayushman Bharat - PMJAY)?', 'Providing health insurance coverage of up to Rs 5 lakh per family per year for secondary/tertiary hospital care', ['Free outpatient dental checkups exclusively', 'Health insurance covering only cosmetic surgeries', 'Life insurance of Rs 50 lakh for government employees'], 'PMJAY provides a cashless safety net of Rs 5 lakh per family per year to bottom 40% vulnerable households.'), ('The Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) legally guarantees how many days of wage employment?', 'At least 100 days of guaranteed wage employment per financial year', ['150 days in all urban areas', '60 days of seasonal farm labor', '365 days of salaried employment'], 'MGNREGA guarantees 100 days of unskilled manual work to every rural household whose adult members volunteer.'), ('What is the core target of the Jal Jeevan Mission (Har Ghar Jal) launched by the Government of India?', 'Providing functional household tap connections (FHTC) of 55 liters per capita daily to all rural households', ['Building irrigation canals in desert areas only', 'Bottling mineral drinking water for railway stations', 'Digging tubewells for private golf courses'], 'Jal Jeevan Mission ensures potable piped water supply at the service level of 55 lpcd to every rural home.'), ('What is the maximum overdraft facility provided to eligible account holders under the Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY)?', 'Rs 10,000', ['Rs 5,000', 'Rs 25,000', 'Rs 50,000'], 'PMJDY accounts offer an overdraft facility of up to Rs 10,000 to one adult member per household (preferably women).'), ('Under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY), what premium rate is paid by farmers for food grain and oilseed Kharif crops?', '2.0% of the sum insured', ['1.5% of sum insured', '5.0% of sum insured', '10.0% of sum insured'], 'Farmers pay a uniform maximum premium of 2.0% for Kharif crops, 1.5% for Rabi crops, and 5.0% for commercial/horticultural crops.'), ('Under PMFBY, what is the maximum premium rate payable by farmers for Rabi crops?', '1.5% of the sum insured', ['2.0% of sum insured', '3.0% of sum insured', '5.0% of sum insured'], "For all Rabi food grain and oilseed crops, the farmer's premium share is capped at 1.5% of the sum insured."), ('Under PMFBY, what is the maximum premium rate payable by farmers for annual commercial and horticultural crops?', '5.0% of the sum insured', ['1.5% of sum insured', '2.0% of sum insured', '8.0% of sum insured'], 'For annual commercial and horticultural crops, the farmer pays a maximum premium of 5.0% of sum insured.'), ('What does the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY) provide to women from below poverty line households?', 'Deposit-free LPG cooking gas connections with financial assistance', ['Free electric induction cooking stoves', 'Subsidized kerosene fuel coupons', 'Monthly cash payments for firewood'], 'PMUY replaces smoky biomass with clean LPG fuel, improving maternal and respiratory health.'), ('Under the PM SVANidhi scheme, who are the targeted primary beneficiaries?', 'Urban street vendors and hawkers', ['Commercial real estate developers', 'Large corporate pharmaceutical firms', 'Software exports multinational enterprises'], 'PM SVANidhi provides affordable collateral-free working capital micro-credit to urban street vendors.'), ('What initial collateral-free working capital loan amount is provided in the first tranche under PM SVANidhi?', 'Up to Rs 10,000', ['Up to Rs 50,000', 'Up to Rs 5,000', 'Up to Rs 1,00,000'], 'Vendors are eligible for an initial loan of up to Rs 10,000, followed by enhanced tranches of Rs 20,000 and Rs 50,000 upon timely repayment.'), ("Under the PM Mudra Yojana (PMMY), what is the loan limit under the 'Shishu' category?", 'Loans up to Rs 50,000', ['Loans from Rs 50,000 to Rs 5 lakh', 'Loans from Rs 5 lakh to Rs 10 lakh', 'Loans above Rs 10 lakh'], 'MUDRA categorizes loans into Shishu (up to Rs 50,000), Kishore (Rs 50,000 to Rs 5 lakh), and Tarun (Rs 5 lakh to Rs 10 lakh).'), ("Under the PM Mudra Yojana (PMMY), what is the loan limit under the 'Kishore' category?", 'Loans above Rs 50,000 and up to Rs 5 lakh', ['Loans up to Rs 50,000', 'Loans from Rs 5 lakh to Rs 10 lakh', 'Loans up to Rs 20 lakh'], 'Kishore loans cater to growing small business enterprises requiring capital between Rs 50,000 and Rs 5 lakh.'), ("Under the PM Mudra Yojana (PMMY), what is the loan limit under the 'Tarun' category?", 'Loans above Rs 5 lakh and up to Rs 10 lakh', ['Loans up to Rs 50,000', 'Loans from Rs 50,000 to Rs 2 lakh', 'Loans above Rs 20 lakh'], 'Tarun loans provide working capital and asset financing from Rs 5 lakh up to Rs 10 lakh for established enterprises.'), ('The Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana (SSY) is a small savings scheme specifically dedicated to the financial security of:', 'The girl child (opened for girls below 10 years of age)', ['Senior citizens above 75 years', 'Unemployed youth seeking foreign visas', 'Commercial taxi drivers'], 'SSY under Beti Bachao Beti Padhao offers high tax-exempt interest for education and marriage of girls.'), ("What is the primary objective of the 'Beti Bachao, Beti Padhao' (BBBP) flagship initiative?", 'Preventing gender-biased sex selection and ensuring survival, protection, and education of the girl child', ['Providing free beauty parlor training', 'Arranging overseas destination weddings', 'Distributing free smartphones to all boys'], "BBBP addresses declining Child Sex Ratio (CSR) and promotes girls' education through inter-ministerial convergence."), ('The Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana - National Rural Livelihoods Mission (DAY-NRLM) organizes rural women into:', 'Self-Help Groups (SHGs) and federations for sustainable livelihoods', ['Political campaign committees', 'Military infantry battalions', 'State road transport corporations'], 'DAY-NRLM mobilizes rural poor women into thrift-and-credit SHGs to access formal bank linkages.'), ('What is the primary mandate of the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY)?', 'Providing all-weather road connectivity to unconnected rural habitations', ['Constructing four-lane expressways between metropolises', 'Paving airport runways in state capitals', 'Building underground metro rail lines'], 'Launched in 2000, PMGSY provides durable paved asphalt road connectivity to eligible rural habitations.'), ('Under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - Gramin (PMAY-G), what financial assistance is provided per housing unit in plain areas?', 'Rs 1.20 lakh per unit', ['Rs 50,000 per unit', 'Rs 2.50 lakh per unit', 'Rs 5.00 lakh per unit'], 'PMAY-G provides Rs 1.20 lakh in plain areas and Rs 1.30 lakh in hilly/difficult/northeastern states.'), ('The Swachh Bharat Mission - Gramin (SBM-G) achieved its initial milestone by declaring rural India:', 'Open Defecation Free (ODF)', ['100% Electrified', '100% Digitally Literate', 'Free from all infectious diseases'], 'SBM-G built over 100 million household toilets, achieving Open Defecation Free status in October 2019.'), ("What does the 'ODF Plus' status under Swachh Bharat Mission Phase II signify?", 'Sustaining ODF status while implementing solid and liquid waste management (SLWM) in villages', ['Distributing free chemical fertilizers to all farmers', 'Constructing municipal swimming pools', 'Providing free broadband internet to village schools'], 'ODF Plus focuses on visual cleanliness, greywater management, plastic waste management, and ODF sustainability.'), ("The 'Stand-Up India' scheme facilitates bank loans between Rs 10 lakh and Rs 1 crore to:", 'At least one SC or ST borrower and at least one woman borrower per bank branch', ['All foreign multinational technology companies', 'Public sector undertaking executives exclusively', 'Large real estate commercial corporations'], 'Stand-Up India promotes greenfield entrepreneurship among SC, ST, and women founders in manufacturing and services.'), ("The 'Atal Pension Yojana' (APY) provides a guaranteed minimum monthly pension ranging from:", 'Rs 1,000 to Rs 5,000 per month starting at age 60', ['Rs 10,000 to Rs 20,000 per month', 'Rs 500 per year', 'Rs 50,000 per month unconditionally'], 'APY targets unorganized sector workers aged 18-40, providing guaranteed post-retirement monthly pensions.'), ('Under the Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY), what is the annual accidental death and disability insurance cover?', 'Rs 2 lakh for accidental death and permanent total disability', ['Rs 10 lakh for natural illness death', 'Rs 50,000 for hospital OPD bills', 'Rs 1 crore for foreign flight accidents'], 'PMSBY provides affordable accidental death and disability insurance of Rs 2 lakh for an annual premium of Rs 20.'), ('Under the Pradhan Mantri Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY), what is the life insurance cover provided upon death due to any cause?', 'Rs 2 lakh life insurance cover', ['Rs 5 lakh life insurance cover', 'Rs 50,000 life insurance cover', 'Rs 10 lakh life insurance cover'], 'PMJJBY offers renewable one-year term life cover of Rs 2 lakh to individuals aged 18-50 for any cause of death.'), ("The 'PM Vishwakarma Scheme' launched in 2023 provides holistic institutional support to:", 'Traditional artisans, craftspeople, and tradespeople working with their hands and tools', ['Software artificial intelligence engineers', 'Commercial airline pilots', 'Investment banker equity brokers'], 'PM Vishwakarma offers skill training, modern toolkit incentive of Rs 15,000, and collateral-free enterprise credit.'), ("The 'PM POSHAN' scheme (formerly known as the Mid-Day Meal Scheme) provides:", 'Hot cooked nutritious lunch to children studying in government and aided primary/upper-primary schools', ['Monthly cash allowances to private school teachers', 'Packaged carbonated beverages to teenagers', 'Free uniforms to university graduate students'], 'PM POSHAN enhances enrollment, retention, and nutritional status among school children across India.'), ("The 'Soil Health Card' scheme provides farmers with customized report cards evaluating:", '12 soil nutrient parameters (macro, secondary, and micro nutrients, plus physical parameters)', ['Only the moisture depth of groundwater aquifers', 'Satellite GPS boundaries of private agricultural land', 'The market selling price of commercial pesticides'], 'Soil health cards analyze N, P, K, S, Zn, Fe, Cu, Mn, Bo, pH, EC, and Organic Carbon to guide balanced fertilizer use.'), ('The electronic trading platform connecting agricultural mandis across states into a unified national market is:', 'e-NAM (National Agriculture Market)', ['GeM Portal', 'PRAGATI Portal', 'Bhavantar Portal'], 'e-NAM integrates APMC mandis to facilitate online competitive bidding, transparent price discovery, and online payments.'), ("The 'Mission Indradhanush' launched by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare aims at:", 'Full immunization coverage for all unvaccinated and partially vaccinated children and pregnant women', ['Constructing solar energy parks in tribal districts', 'Building rainbow bridges over Himalayan rivers', 'Providing free color television sets to rural clinics'], 'Mission Indradhanush targets universal immunization against 12 vaccine-preventable life-threatening diseases.'), ("The 'PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana' launched in 2024 aims to provide free electricity to households by:", 'Subsidizing rooftop solar installations providing up to 300 units of free power monthly for 1 crore homes', ['Distributing free diesel electricity generators', 'Abolishing all electricity billing across commercial factories', 'Connecting homes directly to nuclear reactors'], 'PM Surya Ghar promotes clean energy, saves household power bills, and generates surplus income from grid export.'), ("The 'Smart Cities Mission' launched in 2015 selected how many cities across India for comprehensive urban modernization?", '100 Smart Cities', ['50 Smart Cities', '500 Smart Cities', '20 Smart Cities'], '100 cities were selected through competitive challenge to develop core infrastructure and Integrated Command and Control Centers.'), ("The 'AMRUT' urban mission focuses specifically on providing basic civic infrastructure relating to:", 'Water supply, sewerage, septage management, storm water drainage, and non-motorized urban transport', ['Constructing luxury five-star international hotels', 'Operating commercial passenger airline routes', 'Digitizing corporate stock market exchanges'], 'AMRUT (Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation) covers 500 cities ensuring universal tap water and sewer lines.'), ("The 'PM eBus Sewa' scheme launched by the Union Government aims to deploy:", '10,000 electric buses on Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model in eligible cities', ['50,000 diesel passenger buses', '1,000 luxury helicopter shuttle services', 'Free battery electric scooters to all college students'], 'PM eBus Sewa augments city bus operations with environmentally sustainable electric buses and green transit infrastructure.')]
